  <title>SET OPTIMIZE Command (FoxPro)</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>SET commands</keyword>
    <keyword>SET OPTIMIZE command</keyword>
    <keyword>SET OPTIMIZE command<keyword>FoxPro</keyword></keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SET OPTIMIZE Command &#160;(FoxPro)</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Enables or disables Rushmore optimization. This is the FoxPro version of the <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_OPTIMIZE">SET OPTIMIZE</link> command.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SET OPTIMIZE ON | OFF | &amp;&lt;cMacro&gt;</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ON | OFF<tab />ON enables the optimization of filters and conditions with the open orders. OFF disables it. The value may also be a macro (&amp;) that evaluates to ON or OFF.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">The command changes the same runtime setting as the generic command. The setting is only used by RDDs that support optimization.</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibVFP" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_OPTIMIZE">SET OPTIMIZE</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_FILTER">SET FILTER</link></para>
  </body>
</topic>
